1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:04,963
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:12,971 --> 00:00:14,681
[Ivy] <i>I'll make them pay.</i>

3
00:00:14,764 --> 00:00:18,893
<i>Hello, Poblacion Ardiente. I'm back.</i>

4
00:00:20,311 --> 00:00:21,771
<i>Who is she?</i>

5
00:00:21,855 --> 00:00:25,316
[Pandoy] <i>Our champion, Diego Ardiente…</i>

6
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:26,568
<i>It's Diego, my best friend.</i>

7
00:00:26,651 --> 00:00:28,862
<i>-Yes?</i>
<i>-For you.</i>

8
00:00:29,446 --> 00:00:31,114
<i>Thank you.</i>

9
00:00:31,197 --> 00:00:34,784
[Julio] <i>That's where</i>
<i>your interest lies. Rolling in mud.</i>

10
00:00:34,868 --> 00:00:36,911
<i>Like I told you once before,</i>

11
00:00:36,995 --> 00:00:41,624
<i>some people are only</i>
<i>meant to be worker ants.</i>

12
00:00:41,708 --> 00:00:44,919
<i>I guess that's all you are.</i>

13
00:00:45,003 --> 00:00:46,629
[Diego] <i>I think it's better.</i>

14
00:00:46,713 --> 00:00:49,174
<i>At least one Ardiente</i>
<i>can stand with the people.</i>

15
00:00:49,257 --> 00:00:52,886
[Dante] <i>I want you to learn</i>
<i>how to protect yourself</i>

16
00:00:52,969 --> 00:00:55,847
<i>because your Mom and I</i>
<i>won't always be by your side.</i>

17
00:00:55,930 --> 00:01:00,852
<i>I promise, I will not leave this town</i>

18
00:01:00,935 --> 00:01:05,982
<i>until I find out why this happened.</i>

19
00:01:06,066 --> 00:01:09,110
[Diego] <i>I know Lily will</i>
<i>come back someday. I can feel it.</i>

20
00:01:09,194 --> 00:01:10,361
<i>She'll come back.</i>

21
00:01:10,445 --> 00:01:13,073
[Ivy] <i>Emilia is the key</i>
<i>to what happened to Mom.</i>

22
00:01:13,156 --> 00:01:18,036
<i>But you? You are the key to Emilia.</i>
<i>I'll start with you.</i>

23
00:01:29,422 --> 00:01:33,718
[tense music playing]

24
00:01:51,319 --> 00:01:54,531
[gunshots nearby]

25
00:02:54,591 --> 00:02:56,676
Hold it. Relax, I won't do anything.

26
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:03,391
Looks like you wasted a bullet.
Didn't capture anything?

27
00:03:03,474 --> 00:03:04,726
Bad day, I guess.

28
00:03:04,809 --> 00:03:06,102
[scoffs]

29
00:03:07,645 --> 00:03:08,897
Do you know you're trespassing?

30
00:03:09,647 --> 00:03:12,442
This is private property.
You're a new face.

31
00:03:13,443 --> 00:03:15,528
I know everyone who lives in my town.

32
00:03:20,074 --> 00:03:22,702
I'm Mayor Arnaldo Ardiente-Torillo.

33
00:03:24,370 --> 00:03:25,246
Wow.

34
00:03:25,997 --> 00:03:30,710
Mr. Mayor Arnaldo Ardiente-Torillo.

35
00:03:31,794 --> 00:03:33,254
[scoffs]

36
00:03:33,338 --> 00:03:34,964
I guess it's not a bad day.

37
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:37,133
I spotted the right person

38
00:03:37,759 --> 00:03:40,511
who can guide me in this little town.

39
00:03:41,596 --> 00:03:44,849
Mr. Mayor, my name is Ivy.

40
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:47,352
Ivy Aguas.

41
00:03:49,979 --> 00:03:53,399
[tense music playing]

42
00:04:09,874 --> 00:04:13,503
Mr. Mayor, I saw on your
website that you're looking for investors.

43
00:04:14,504 --> 00:04:17,757
But other than this forest for hunting,

44
00:04:17,840 --> 00:04:22,011
I don't see any exceptional opportunities.

45
00:04:23,304 --> 00:04:24,430
That's pretty blunt.

46
00:04:25,598 --> 00:04:27,767
No mayor wants to hear things like that.

47
00:04:28,351 --> 00:04:31,104
Oh, I'm sorry, Mr. Mayor,
but I call it as I see it.

48
00:04:31,187 --> 00:04:33,273
Maybe you need to look closer.

49
00:04:34,399 --> 00:04:37,902
Ms. Ivy Aguas, let me show you around.

50
00:04:38,569 --> 00:04:42,198
Maybe I can change
how you look at my little town.

51
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:45,243
We'll see, Mr. Mayor.

52
00:04:45,827 --> 00:04:48,830
Well, I have to go. Happy hunting.

53
00:04:49,580 --> 00:04:52,500
[action music playing]

54
00:05:11,519 --> 00:05:14,814
Sweetie! Where have you been all day?

55
00:05:14,897 --> 00:05:17,734
When I woke up, you were gone.
What happened?

56
00:05:17,817 --> 00:05:20,153
Nanny, have you eaten yet?
Get dressed, and let's eat.

57
00:05:20,236 --> 00:05:21,904
Where have you been?

58
00:05:23,281 --> 00:05:24,407
Nanny Carlotta.

59
00:05:25,116 --> 00:05:26,701
I've laid the trap.

60
00:05:26,784 --> 00:05:31,164
All we need is for him
to walk right into it.

61
00:05:34,083 --> 00:05:40,131
I'm sure that Mayor Ardiente
will be here tomorrow.

62
00:05:40,715 --> 00:05:44,302
And when that happens, I must be ready.

63
00:05:45,219 --> 00:05:46,345
Let's go.

64
00:05:46,429 --> 00:05:47,638
Dear…

65
00:06:01,569 --> 00:06:02,695
Here, Mayor.

66
00:06:09,368 --> 00:06:10,787
[action music playing]

67
00:06:11,496 --> 00:06:13,664
That's all the information
I got as of now.

68
00:06:13,748 --> 00:06:17,168
But if we look at the status
of her assets,

69
00:06:17,251 --> 00:06:19,462
she can be an investor here in Ardiente.

70
00:06:20,296 --> 00:06:22,757
Good work. You're very reliable.

71
00:06:42,068 --> 00:06:44,070
[upbeat music playing]

72
00:07:32,452 --> 00:07:35,121
[upbeat music continues playing]

73
00:07:57,435 --> 00:07:59,061
I knew I'd find you here.

74
00:08:04,859 --> 00:08:05,943
Mr. Mayor.

75
00:08:09,238 --> 00:08:10,198
What brings you here?

76
00:08:10,281 --> 00:08:13,826
I wanted to change
your perception of Ardiente.

77
00:08:15,995 --> 00:08:21,167
Oh, no. It might be hard.

78
00:08:22,960 --> 00:08:24,587
Please…

79
00:08:25,171 --> 00:08:27,924
Humor me. You're here, anyway.

80
00:08:30,134 --> 00:08:31,886
Let me give you the grand tour.

81
00:08:33,012 --> 00:08:36,933
After that, if you're still not convinced…

82
00:08:41,312 --> 00:08:43,356
at least, you can say…

83
00:08:44,815 --> 00:08:46,150
you tried.

84
00:08:47,443 --> 00:08:48,819
No regrets.

85
00:08:54,909 --> 00:08:59,705
Now you're making it hard
for me, Mr. Mayor.

86
00:08:59,789 --> 00:09:00,831
[Ivy] Oops.

87
00:09:01,415 --> 00:09:03,960
[Arnaldo] Please, let me.

88
00:09:11,425 --> 00:09:15,346
[upbeat music playing]

89
00:09:38,411 --> 00:09:42,039
[Ivy] Mr. Mayor.
You didn't have to fetch me.

90
00:09:42,123 --> 00:09:45,543
I have my own car, and I can drive.

91
00:09:46,294 --> 00:09:48,546
I know. But where's the fun in that?

92
00:09:51,465 --> 00:09:52,633
This is Madrigal.

93
00:09:52,717 --> 00:09:55,720
He's my most trusted man.
He'll accompany us.

94
00:09:59,348 --> 00:10:00,725
Just him?

95
00:10:00,808 --> 00:10:04,103
You don't have
any other bodyguards besides him?

96
00:10:07,064 --> 00:10:11,277
Well, we don't need that many
bodyguards where we're going.

97
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:15,656
And if I need to, I can protect you.

98
00:10:17,783 --> 00:10:18,701
Shall we?

99
00:10:35,718 --> 00:10:38,971
[upbeat music playing]

100
00:10:40,222 --> 00:10:41,057
[Arnaldo] Um…

101
00:10:41,140 --> 00:10:44,185
The first stop is the school
that our family built.

102
00:10:44,268 --> 00:10:45,686
We're still expanding the building

103
00:10:45,770 --> 00:10:48,397
so we can take in more students.

104
00:10:49,732 --> 00:10:52,276
This hospital
is one of the highlights of the town.

105
00:10:52,360 --> 00:10:54,487
An Ardiente was the one
who had it built too.

106
00:10:55,404 --> 00:10:56,364
My grandfather, actually.

107
00:10:56,447 --> 00:10:58,908
We're well-equipped enough
that we can compete

108
00:10:58,991 --> 00:11:00,618
with the hospitals in Manila.

109
00:11:03,329 --> 00:11:06,791
Oh. Check that out. That one right there.

110
00:11:06,874 --> 00:11:08,793
-What? What's--
-That. That church.

111
00:11:13,672 --> 00:11:17,051
Mr. Mayor, I didn't know we were close.

112
00:11:19,595 --> 00:11:20,596
Sorry.

113
00:11:25,017 --> 00:11:28,979
Ivy. See that? That statue.

114
00:11:34,193 --> 00:11:35,694
That's my grandfather.

115
00:11:36,445 --> 00:11:39,782
I remember there was a feast
when it was erected.

116
00:11:39,865 --> 00:11:41,242
I was still a kid.

117
00:11:45,996 --> 00:11:50,751
As long as this statue
stands firm in our town,

118
00:11:50,835 --> 00:11:56,006
you will continue to have
honest service and leadership!

119
00:11:56,090 --> 00:12:00,261
-[Julio] Viva Ardiente!
-[crowd] Viva Ardiente!

120
00:12:11,939 --> 00:12:13,107
Who's that man?

121
00:12:18,028 --> 00:12:20,906
Oh, him? He was already like that

122
00:12:20,990 --> 00:12:23,701
when I came back from studying in America.

123
00:12:24,285 --> 00:12:26,370
They say he just went mad one day

124
00:12:26,454 --> 00:12:29,915
and began living on the streets.
He doesn't have a family.

125
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:33,002
They say he disappears from time to time.

126
00:12:33,085 --> 00:12:35,379
Then suddenly shows up again at the plaza.

127
00:12:37,590 --> 00:12:39,133
It was him! Him!

128
00:12:41,635 --> 00:12:44,263
-Him!
-He'll leave town and then come back.

129
00:12:44,930 --> 00:12:47,183
But don't worry. He's harmless.

130
00:12:48,517 --> 00:12:50,102
-He's pure evil!
-[woman] Hey, nutcase!

131
00:12:50,186 --> 00:12:53,731
-[woman exclaims] Move along!
-You go away!

132
00:12:53,814 --> 00:12:55,441
[wailing]

133
00:12:56,025 --> 00:12:56,942
Let's go, Madrigal.

134
00:13:02,156 --> 00:13:05,242
[Arthur] No! No! Stop!

135
00:13:05,326 --> 00:13:08,412
Wait!

136
00:13:21,175 --> 00:13:23,511
Okay, I'm gonna show you everything.

137
00:13:23,594 --> 00:13:25,513
Or you might say I'm biased

138
00:13:25,596 --> 00:13:28,933
because I just showed you
the nice parts of the town.

139
00:13:30,142 --> 00:13:33,187
You know… I was thinking.

140
00:13:33,270 --> 00:13:38,400
For a mayor, you've got lots of free time.

141
00:13:39,276 --> 00:13:40,861
I cleared my schedule for you.

142
00:13:46,242 --> 00:13:50,287
[upbeat music playing]

143
00:13:52,581 --> 00:13:54,166
[Ivy laughing]

144
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:59,380
Mr. Mayor, I didn't expect you
to be such a comedian.

145
00:13:59,964 --> 00:14:01,340
I have my moments.

146
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:06,053
[Loring] Get an inventory
of those vegetables!

147
00:14:06,136 --> 00:14:09,431
Don't forget the prices!
We have to… Okay, good.

148
00:14:09,515 --> 00:14:10,558
[Diego] Here, sir.

149
00:14:11,475 --> 00:14:13,227
[Loring] Yes. Shouldn't that
be shipped already?

150
00:14:13,310 --> 00:14:14,728
-Here.
-Are we almost done?

151
00:14:14,812 --> 00:14:16,021
-Yeah.
-We're almost done.

152
00:14:16,105 --> 00:14:18,732
Sir, how are you holding up?
Are you still okay?

153
00:14:18,816 --> 00:14:21,235
-Why wouldn't I be? We're both fit!
-[Diego chuckles]

154
00:14:21,318 --> 00:14:25,656
You? I don't see any muscles!
You're getting pale!

155
00:14:25,739 --> 00:14:28,325
You need fresh air!
You need to build some muscle!

156
00:14:28,409 --> 00:14:32,413
Build some muscle? Come here!
I'll show you some muscle!

157
00:14:32,496 --> 00:14:33,372
[Loring laughs]

158
00:14:33,455 --> 00:14:36,166
You missed this, didn't you?
See? You're wrong!

159
00:14:36,250 --> 00:14:38,168
-It's Arnaldo!
-What?

160
00:14:38,752 --> 00:14:39,920
We're here. Mayor.

161
00:14:40,004 --> 00:14:43,716
[suspenseful music playing]

162
00:14:45,509 --> 00:14:46,427
Mayor.

163
00:14:47,428 --> 00:14:49,013
May I talk to you for a while?

164
00:14:49,096 --> 00:14:49,930
Okay.

165
00:14:51,140 --> 00:14:52,808
-Excuse me.
-Sure.

166
00:15:00,733 --> 00:15:02,735
-Why?
-I need to leave for a bit, Mayor.

167
00:15:02,818 --> 00:15:05,946
-Where are you going?
-I need to take care

168
00:15:06,030 --> 00:15:07,406
of the property
you want to show our guest.

169
00:15:07,489 --> 00:15:09,074
Okay, we can't afford
to make any mistakes.

170
00:15:09,158 --> 00:15:10,576
Yes, Mayor.

171
00:15:21,045 --> 00:15:22,963
[man] Because it's cold
in the office and in the car.

172
00:15:26,175 --> 00:15:27,176
Thank you.

173
00:15:28,344 --> 00:15:29,887
-[man] Who's that?
-[Loring] Oh.

174
00:15:30,638 --> 00:15:32,723
["Sa'Yo" instrumental playing]

175
00:15:32,806 --> 00:15:33,724
[Loring] Oh.

176
00:15:33,807 --> 00:15:36,226
-It's her…
-Oh, yeah.

177
00:15:36,810 --> 00:15:37,895
[Arnaldo] Let's go?

178
00:15:58,958 --> 00:16:01,418
-Diego has a huge crush on her.
-Oh…

179
00:16:02,711 --> 00:16:03,629
Let's go?

180
00:16:04,672 --> 00:16:05,673
Yeah.

181
00:16:06,465 --> 00:16:08,884
[Loring] She was the woman
I told you about before.

182
00:16:08,968 --> 00:16:10,177
Let's welcome them!

183
00:16:13,263 --> 00:16:14,223
[Arnaldo] Good day!

184
00:16:14,306 --> 00:16:15,933
-Good morning!
-Mayor!

185
00:16:16,016 --> 00:16:17,685
-Mayor.
-Good day, Mayor!

186
00:16:17,768 --> 00:16:19,561
Nice to see you here today.

187
00:16:19,645 --> 00:16:24,775
Yes, I'm just showing our guest
around Ardiente.

188
00:16:24,858 --> 00:16:29,655
I want her to see
all the beautiful places in this town.

189
00:16:30,489 --> 00:16:34,493
And above all, I want her
to meet all you hardworking people.

190
00:16:34,576 --> 00:16:37,663
They are the cooperative of the workers

191
00:16:37,746 --> 00:16:39,581
and farmers of this town.

192
00:16:40,290 --> 00:16:41,625
This is Mr. Fernan.

193
00:16:41,709 --> 00:16:43,585
-Good morning.
-He leads this group.

194
00:16:43,669 --> 00:16:46,505
Along with Mr. Pandoy and Mrs. Loring.

195
00:16:48,007 --> 00:16:52,219
And this is my brother, Diego.

196
00:16:53,178 --> 00:16:56,932
He helped Mr. Pandoy
form this cooperative.

197
00:16:59,435 --> 00:17:02,730
["Sa'Yo" instrumental playing]

198
00:17:02,813 --> 00:17:03,939
Diego.

199
00:17:20,914 --> 00:17:22,666
Ivy Aguas.

200
00:17:28,088 --> 00:17:29,798
[clears throat]

201
00:17:29,882 --> 00:17:31,592
What are you doing here, Diego?

202
00:17:34,803 --> 00:17:38,140
I'm always here… helping the people.

203
00:17:42,227 --> 00:17:45,105
Ivy! So that's your name.

204
00:17:45,189 --> 00:17:48,233
-Mr. Pandoy.
-Yes, it's Mr. Pandoy. Uh…

205
00:17:48,317 --> 00:17:54,073
We've been wondering
who the beautiful tourist was.

206
00:17:54,156 --> 00:17:56,325
[stutters] You've met?

207
00:17:56,408 --> 00:17:57,493
[Loring] Oh…

208
00:17:57,576 --> 00:18:01,330
Mayor, I was trying
to sell her some fritters,

209
00:18:01,413 --> 00:18:03,123
but she told me she's on a diet.

210
00:18:03,207 --> 00:18:04,458
-[Pandoy laughs]
-[Loring] Right?

211
00:18:04,541 --> 00:18:07,252
But, ma'am, I didn't cook some today.

212
00:18:07,336 --> 00:18:08,837
I'm afraid you won't be able to try them.

213
00:18:08,921 --> 00:18:12,549
[Pandoy] Too bad! My Loring
cooks the best fritters!

214
00:18:12,633 --> 00:18:14,384
Maybe next time.

215
00:18:14,468 --> 00:18:16,637
Sorry, Mayor, I didn't cook today.

216
00:18:16,720 --> 00:18:19,056
I didn't know you were coming.

217
00:18:19,139 --> 00:18:21,892
Oh, that's all right. Like what Ivy said,

218
00:18:21,975 --> 00:18:25,145
we can try it next time.
We won't stay long here anyway.

219
00:18:25,229 --> 00:18:26,647
We still have other places to see.

220
00:18:26,730 --> 00:18:28,524
So, we'll be on our way!

221
00:18:28,607 --> 00:18:30,609
-Thanks for dropping by.
-All right.

222
00:18:30,692 --> 00:18:31,693
-Thank you, Mayor!
-All right.

223
00:18:31,777 --> 00:18:33,403
-Nice meeting you all.
-You too.

224
00:18:33,487 --> 00:18:34,905
[Pandoy] Ms. Ivy…

225
00:18:34,988 --> 00:18:36,406
-[Loring] Enjoy your stay!
-Let's go.

226
00:18:38,784 --> 00:18:41,036
COOPERATIVE OF FARMERS
AND WORKERS OF ARDIENTE

227
00:18:43,872 --> 00:18:48,043
So that pretty woman is the Mayor's guest!

228
00:18:48,127 --> 00:18:49,461
[Pandoy chuckles]

229
00:18:49,545 --> 00:18:55,217
But I don't think the Mayor
knows about the flowers

230
00:18:55,300 --> 00:18:58,303
you gave at the tournament.

231
00:18:58,387 --> 00:18:59,429
Right, Diego?

232
00:19:01,140 --> 00:19:02,432
[Pandoy chuckles]

233
00:19:04,685 --> 00:19:08,814
So, where are you
taking me next, Mr. Mayor?

234
00:19:08,897 --> 00:19:11,984
The next place we're going to
has something you can only find

235
00:19:12,067 --> 00:19:13,318
in this region of the country.

236
00:19:14,653 --> 00:19:15,612
Let's see.

237
00:19:20,701 --> 00:19:22,286
["Sa'Yo" by Silent Sanctuary playing]

238
00:19:41,471 --> 00:19:44,808
[tense music playing]

239
00:19:53,358 --> 00:19:54,526
[Ivy] So…

240
00:19:55,402 --> 00:19:56,486
Why are we here?

241
00:20:00,407 --> 00:20:02,576
Well… My grandfather…

242
00:20:03,202 --> 00:20:05,495
Congressman Julio Ardiente…

243
00:20:06,413 --> 00:20:08,999
had these windmills installed.

244
00:20:09,791 --> 00:20:13,962
In this region, this is the only town
that can generate its own electricity.

245
00:20:14,588 --> 00:20:18,217
If the region has a blackout,
it won't affect Poblacion.

246
00:20:18,300 --> 00:20:19,843
And now…

247
00:20:20,844 --> 00:20:21,887
we all know…

248
00:20:22,971 --> 00:20:26,058
renewable energy is big these days.

249
00:20:31,355 --> 00:20:32,231
So…

250
00:20:33,607 --> 00:20:35,317
Impressed yet?

251
00:20:41,448 --> 00:20:42,574
Wow!

252
00:20:43,200 --> 00:20:44,451
Wow.

253
00:20:45,035 --> 00:20:46,828
That was my best shot!

254
00:20:47,537 --> 00:20:48,413
Those?

255
00:20:48,497 --> 00:20:52,000
I already saw those when I arrived.

256
00:20:53,252 --> 00:20:55,462
Mr. Mayor, I thought…

257
00:20:55,545 --> 00:20:58,173
you wanted to change
my opinion of this town?

258
00:20:58,840 --> 00:21:00,133
Of your town.

259
00:21:00,801 --> 00:21:02,094
Are you giving up?

260
00:21:02,177 --> 00:21:05,222
Oh, Ms. Aguas.

261
00:21:05,889 --> 00:21:11,812
I don't easily give up.

262
00:21:13,855 --> 00:21:16,733
So, if I really can't convince you…

263
00:21:18,860 --> 00:21:20,570
can we just enjoy the rest of the day?

264
00:21:26,535 --> 00:21:27,452
I guess so.

265
00:21:28,620 --> 00:21:29,788
Well then…

266
00:21:33,792 --> 00:21:35,669
[Arnaldo chuckles]

267
00:21:46,847 --> 00:21:52,728
Mr. Mayor, I thought you were
looking for investors.

268
00:21:54,646 --> 00:21:58,734
If you want to go on a date
with me, you could've just asked.

269
00:21:59,609 --> 00:22:00,569
I'm a hunter.

270
00:22:02,029 --> 00:22:04,656
I like hitting two birds with one stone.

271
00:22:08,535 --> 00:22:09,661
[chuckles]

272
00:22:13,832 --> 00:22:15,000
[exhales]

273
00:22:18,462 --> 00:22:21,506
[suspenseful music playing]

274
00:22:25,218 --> 00:22:26,595
Whose house is that?

275
00:22:35,020 --> 00:22:38,774
I said… Whose house is that?

276
00:22:38,857 --> 00:22:41,985
[upbeat music playing]

277
00:22:59,836 --> 00:23:03,006
I already paid
the reservation fee for this house.

278
00:23:05,133 --> 00:23:06,676
But I can get a refund.

279
00:23:07,928 --> 00:23:10,055
You can have this property.

280
00:23:11,598 --> 00:23:12,766
If you want it.

281
00:23:16,394 --> 00:23:17,938
And it comes with the lake.

282
00:23:21,483 --> 00:23:22,651
[Arnaldo exhales]

283
00:23:26,947 --> 00:23:28,156
[chuckles]

284
00:23:28,240 --> 00:23:30,408
I get it. You planned this.

285
00:23:30,492 --> 00:23:34,329
This was the clincher
of your sales pitch for Ardiente.

286
00:23:35,288 --> 00:23:39,084
Fine. I'll admit.
I did my research on you.

287
00:23:40,085 --> 00:23:42,379
I discovered
you have an eye for real estate.

288
00:23:42,462 --> 00:23:45,841
I also learned you don't back down
if a property catches your eye.

289
00:23:46,466 --> 00:23:47,634
And this house…

290
00:23:48,510 --> 00:23:53,223
Let's just say I had
a feeling you'd love it.

291
00:23:53,974 --> 00:23:59,104
I figured, if I can't
convince you to invest in Ardiente…

292
00:23:59,980 --> 00:24:05,861
Well, I can at least give you a reason
to come back every now and then.

293
00:24:05,944 --> 00:24:07,404
Which you will do

294
00:24:08,822 --> 00:24:10,782
if you end up purchasing this house.

295
00:24:14,744 --> 00:24:16,746
You're starting to impress me, Mr. Mayor.

296
00:24:16,830 --> 00:24:20,083
You're giving me reasons…

297
00:24:21,501 --> 00:24:26,631
Reasons to keep coming back here.

298
00:24:29,593 --> 00:24:34,973
So, what will it take, Mr. Mayor, to…

299
00:24:36,016 --> 00:24:38,018
make this property mine?

300
00:24:47,194 --> 00:24:49,571
I want you…

301
00:24:52,240 --> 00:24:54,784
to invest here in Ardiente.

302
00:24:56,786 --> 00:24:59,289
I'm planning to build
an export processing zone…

303
00:24:59,956 --> 00:25:02,834
on the property we visited earlier.

304
00:25:08,632 --> 00:25:12,886
You're complicating things, Mr. Mayor.

305
00:25:17,349 --> 00:25:19,100
Well, you know what they say.

306
00:25:19,726 --> 00:25:23,813
If you want something,
you should know how to get it.

307
00:25:27,067 --> 00:25:28,818
Do we have a deal?

308
00:25:30,987 --> 00:25:33,865
[tense music playing]

309
00:25:41,873 --> 00:25:44,292
You know I want that property badly!

310
00:25:44,960 --> 00:25:47,420
Even if it's just sitting
there waiting for us to take it,

311
00:25:47,504 --> 00:25:48,713
I want that property!

312
00:25:48,797 --> 00:25:51,049
Mom, that property is useless to us!

313
00:25:51,132 --> 00:25:53,301
What do you want it for?
We're not moving out anyway.

314
00:25:53,385 --> 00:25:57,097
That's not my point!
My point is I want that house!

315
00:25:57,180 --> 00:26:00,141
It's our house! It's mine! All mine!

316
00:26:02,727 --> 00:26:03,687
Grandpa.

317
00:26:07,190 --> 00:26:10,443
[tense music playing]

318
00:26:11,027 --> 00:26:12,904
[Ivy] Nanny Carlotta…

319
00:26:12,988 --> 00:26:17,075
that house was previously owned
by their political rival.

320
00:26:17,659 --> 00:26:21,913
But the family went bankrupt.
And now they're living abroad.

321
00:26:22,580 --> 00:26:25,250
Same old story. That's how
things work around here.

322
00:26:26,293 --> 00:26:28,586
-Careful, it's hot.
-Thank you.

323
00:26:28,670 --> 00:26:30,755
[Arnaldo] <i>That property is worthless.</i>

324
00:26:31,339 --> 00:26:32,674
Now, what is the reason

325
00:26:32,757 --> 00:26:35,093
why we can't acquire it
in the first place?

326
00:26:35,176 --> 00:26:40,307
We lack funds. All our funds
are allocated for the campaign.

327
00:26:40,390 --> 00:26:44,060
Now think about this.
By sacrificing that property,

328
00:26:44,144 --> 00:26:46,855
we can generate another stream of income.

329
00:26:48,273 --> 00:26:51,151
[Carlotta] When will you move in?

330
00:26:54,863 --> 00:26:56,614
As soon as possible.

331
00:26:57,490 --> 00:27:02,162
As you know, the Ardientes
are strapped for cash.

332
00:27:02,245 --> 00:27:03,705
[chuckles]

333
00:27:03,788 --> 00:27:08,626
I'm sure the mayor
will give me what I want.

334
00:27:11,004 --> 00:27:12,422
-But--
-Arnaldo's right.

335
00:27:13,006 --> 00:27:16,634
We should give up that property.

336
00:27:17,969 --> 00:27:24,059
But as usual, all you ever
care about is spending money.

337
00:27:25,143 --> 00:27:26,019
Arnaldo.

338
00:27:27,520 --> 00:27:29,856
Yours is the right decision.

339
00:27:38,573 --> 00:27:41,034
[Ivy] I told you. I can handle this.

340
00:27:49,626 --> 00:27:53,046
[tense music playing]

341
00:28:01,054 --> 00:28:03,264
[upbeat music playing]

342
00:28:16,694 --> 00:28:20,115
[tense music playing]

343
00:28:32,293 --> 00:28:34,295
[Carlotta] It's so beautiful!

344
00:28:35,713 --> 00:28:37,507
Look at the pool.

345
00:28:37,590 --> 00:28:39,134
[chuckles]

346
00:28:39,718 --> 00:28:41,261
Oh, sweetie.

347
00:28:41,344 --> 00:28:45,890
I called the servants in Manila.
They'll be here soon.

348
00:28:45,974 --> 00:28:48,435
-Thanks, Nanny.
-I'll check the kitchen.

349
00:28:48,518 --> 00:28:50,478
-Okay.
-Are you hungry?

350
00:28:50,562 --> 00:28:52,856
I'm fine. I still have a call to make.

351
00:28:52,939 --> 00:28:54,274
[Carlotta] Okay.

352
00:28:57,444 --> 00:28:58,403
[line ringing]

353
00:28:58,486 --> 00:29:01,573
Yes, Joan? Please deliver the documents

354
00:29:01,656 --> 00:29:04,409
I have to sign here at Poblacion Ardiente.

355
00:29:04,492 --> 00:29:07,454
Just use one of the company cars.

356
00:29:07,537 --> 00:29:11,791
And, um, tell Mr. Sy
I will return his call in an hour.

357
00:29:13,293 --> 00:29:14,711
All right. Thank you.

358
00:29:15,545 --> 00:29:18,923
[pensive music playing]

359
00:29:19,007 --> 00:29:20,216
[sighs]

360
00:29:46,451 --> 00:29:49,037
[Prianka] Always remember this.

361
00:29:49,704 --> 00:29:53,333
Being a woman is both
a blessing and a curse.

362
00:29:55,251 --> 00:29:57,587
It's a double-edged sword, Ivy.

363
00:29:57,670 --> 00:30:01,007
Should you use your femininity
to your advantage,

364
00:30:01,090 --> 00:30:06,846
make sure not to hurt yourself.

365
00:30:08,181 --> 00:30:12,811
You're Ivy Aguas.
To the world, you are my daughter.

366
00:30:13,478 --> 00:30:19,734
You are the heiress to everything I own.

367
00:30:23,154 --> 00:30:27,659
But while I'm still breathing,
I'll make sure

368
00:30:27,742 --> 00:30:33,540
that you learn and earn
to deserve every cent.

369
00:30:33,623 --> 00:30:38,336
You shouldn't just be beautiful.
You should also be tough. Smart.

370
00:30:39,128 --> 00:30:42,382
And your heart should be
in the right place.

371
00:30:43,550 --> 00:30:48,429
If you can't do that,
you'll be back on the streets.

372
00:30:48,513 --> 00:30:49,556
Do you understand me?

373
00:30:52,058 --> 00:30:53,601
Yes, Ms. Prianka.

374
00:31:00,483 --> 00:31:01,818
Beautiful.

375
00:31:08,157 --> 00:31:10,910
[phone ringing]

376
00:31:19,711 --> 00:31:22,005
-Mr. Mayor.
-Dinner.

377
00:31:22,088 --> 00:31:25,174
<i>At my place this weekend.</i>

378
00:31:25,842 --> 00:31:26,759
With the family.

379
00:31:32,432 --> 00:31:33,516
<i>Dinner?</i>

380
00:31:34,309 --> 00:31:36,895
With the family?

381
00:31:37,979 --> 00:31:39,355
Isn't that too fast?

382
00:31:39,439 --> 00:31:42,609
Uh, well, not really.

383
00:31:42,692 --> 00:31:45,486
Because you still call me Mr. Mayor.

384
00:31:46,905 --> 00:31:49,032
When will you call me by my name?

385
00:31:50,199 --> 00:31:51,701
Perhaps…

386
00:31:53,161 --> 00:31:56,247
when I get to know your whole family.

387
00:31:56,331 --> 00:31:57,165
<i>Oh!</i>

388
00:31:58,625 --> 00:32:00,627
Does that mean it's a yes?

389
00:32:01,461 --> 00:32:02,378
Yes, to dinner.

390
00:32:02,462 --> 00:32:04,130
[scoffs]

391
00:32:04,213 --> 00:32:06,174
See you, Mr. Mayor.

392
00:32:20,188 --> 00:32:21,898
[Ivy] I replied to Mr. Teodoro.

393
00:32:21,981 --> 00:32:24,943
I said, "no deal".
I also emailed everyone.

394
00:32:25,026 --> 00:32:29,155
I told them not to entertain him
until he agrees to my terms.

395
00:32:29,238 --> 00:32:31,074
-Joan? Joan!
-Yes, ma'am?

396
00:32:31,157 --> 00:32:32,450
You know what to do.

397
00:32:32,533 --> 00:32:33,576
Yes, ma'am. Noted.

398
00:32:34,160 --> 00:32:37,038
By the way, I brought
everything you need from work.

399
00:32:37,789 --> 00:32:39,165
Okay, thank you.

400
00:32:40,583 --> 00:32:44,003
It's late, you should get going.
You still have to go back to Manila.

401
00:32:44,087 --> 00:32:45,797
I'll just see you next week. Take care.

402
00:32:45,880 --> 00:32:47,256
Yes, Ms. Aguas. Thank you.

403
00:32:48,341 --> 00:32:50,009
[suspenseful music playing]

404
00:32:55,056 --> 00:32:59,060
Sweetie? I prepared some snacks for you.

405
00:32:59,143 --> 00:33:00,728
Thanks, Nanny.

406
00:33:05,316 --> 00:33:06,859
Sweetie?

407
00:33:06,943 --> 00:33:10,905
I'm sure the rest of that family
knows you're here now.

408
00:33:10,989 --> 00:33:12,532
Have they gotten in touch?

409
00:33:17,704 --> 00:33:18,788
Yes, Nanny.

410
00:33:19,414 --> 00:33:20,915
They know.

411
00:33:22,375 --> 00:33:23,918
And tonight…

412
00:33:24,585 --> 00:33:30,133
Ivy Aguas will introduce herself
to the Ardientes.

413
00:33:34,095 --> 00:33:35,179
[chuckles]

414
00:33:36,264 --> 00:33:37,432
How exciting.

415
00:33:38,224 --> 00:33:42,103
[suspenseful music playing]

416
00:33:46,274 --> 00:33:49,027
[Diego] Nanny… Here are the vegetables.

417
00:33:49,110 --> 00:33:51,154
[Loring] Okay. Just put them there.

418
00:33:53,114 --> 00:33:54,282
You know what?

419
00:33:54,949 --> 00:34:00,371
I think Ms. Ivy will be
staying here much longer.

420
00:34:00,455 --> 00:34:04,792
I thought she'd just turn
the mansion she bought

421
00:34:04,876 --> 00:34:06,002
into a vacation house.

422
00:34:06,085 --> 00:34:09,881
But some men went there the other day.

423
00:34:10,631 --> 00:34:13,384
Actually, she's at our house
right now. Arnaldo invited her.

424
00:34:13,468 --> 00:34:17,513
Apparently, it's to formally
welcome her to Ardiente.

425
00:34:18,181 --> 00:34:20,308
Why are you here if she's there?

426
00:34:21,017 --> 00:34:23,561
What? What would I do there?

427
00:34:23,644 --> 00:34:27,857
Oh, come on. Don't you like that Ivy?

428
00:34:27,940 --> 00:34:31,861
Are you going to let
your brother make a move on her?

429
00:34:31,944 --> 00:34:35,448
[Loring] Well, if that woman
is interested in Arnaldo,

430
00:34:35,531 --> 00:34:38,034
then she's not the one for Diego.

431
00:34:39,702 --> 00:34:40,870
You know what, Nanny?

432
00:34:42,497 --> 00:34:46,125
You're right. I should've
given you those flowers.

433
00:34:46,209 --> 00:34:47,585
[Pandoy chuckling]

434
00:34:47,668 --> 00:34:51,672
I knew it! You finally regret it.

435
00:34:51,756 --> 00:34:55,218
But don't worry, dear. I love you.

436
00:34:55,301 --> 00:34:59,305
With all my heart. [giggling]

437
00:35:01,099 --> 00:35:02,225
You know that.

438
00:35:02,308 --> 00:35:05,770
[tense music playing]

439
00:35:32,880 --> 00:35:34,507
This way, Ms. Aguas.

440
00:35:39,095 --> 00:35:42,306
Uh… I'll let them know you're here now.

441
00:35:42,390 --> 00:35:43,307
Thank you.

442
00:35:43,391 --> 00:35:46,894
[dramatic music playing]

443
00:35:56,737 --> 00:35:58,823
[Ivy] <i>I'll find out the truth</i>

444
00:35:58,906 --> 00:36:03,035
<i>about what you had to do</i>
<i>with my mother's death.</i>

445
00:36:03,119 --> 00:36:06,247
[dramatic music playing]

446
00:36:20,511 --> 00:36:23,598
Hi. You must be Ivy.

447
00:36:28,686 --> 00:36:29,687
Yes.

448
00:36:30,813 --> 00:36:33,274
Ivy Aguas.

449
00:36:38,112 --> 00:36:39,780
Governor Emilia Ardiente.

450
00:36:42,992 --> 00:36:43,910
Pleased to meet you.

451
00:36:47,496 --> 00:36:49,582
So, how is your newly acquired property?

452
00:36:50,583 --> 00:36:53,211
Do you know I've been eyeing that house?

453
00:36:54,503 --> 00:36:56,547
What made you give it up, Governor?

454
00:36:58,007 --> 00:37:01,093
Arnaldo convinced me to let you have it.

455
00:37:01,928 --> 00:37:02,762
Awww.

456
00:37:03,596 --> 00:37:06,557
I admire people like you, Governor.

457
00:37:06,641 --> 00:37:09,518
Those who know how to accept defeat.

458
00:37:11,187 --> 00:37:13,189
But I never lose when it matters.

459
00:37:13,272 --> 00:37:15,358
Never? So, this was your first time?

460
00:37:16,901 --> 00:37:20,655
[tense music playing]

461
00:37:21,906 --> 00:37:22,949
Ivy.

462
00:37:23,699 --> 00:37:24,951
-Mr. Mayor.
-Good evening.

463
00:37:27,036 --> 00:37:28,955
You look lovely.

464
00:37:29,705 --> 00:37:31,624
-Hmm. Thank you.
-Well, I can see you met

465
00:37:31,707 --> 00:37:34,710
my mom already. Mom, where's Dad?

466
00:37:34,794 --> 00:37:36,254
-On his way.
-Okay, good.

467
00:37:36,337 --> 00:37:37,880
Grandpa's on his way too.

468
00:37:37,964 --> 00:37:39,966
Shall we wait for them in the dining room?

469
00:37:40,800 --> 00:37:43,386
-Sure.
-Okay, let's go. Shall we?

470
00:37:49,850 --> 00:37:53,896
-Oh. Mom. Coming?
-Sure.

471
00:37:55,439 --> 00:37:59,485
[Julio] Arnaldo's export
zone project is comparable

472
00:37:59,568 --> 00:38:02,780
to my windmill project
during my time as mayor.

473
00:38:03,572 --> 00:38:05,074
That's why I don't see any reason why

474
00:38:05,157 --> 00:38:07,285
you'd refuse my grandson's offer.

475
00:38:07,952 --> 00:38:09,912
[Arnaldo] Easy, Grandpa.

476
00:38:09,996 --> 00:38:13,833
Ivy might think we have
an agenda for inviting her.

477
00:38:14,458 --> 00:38:16,585
It's all right.

478
00:38:16,669 --> 00:38:20,047
Um… Actually, Congressman…

479
00:38:20,131 --> 00:38:23,259
I promised the Mayor I'd invest,

480
00:38:23,342 --> 00:38:27,179
but, of course,
I still have to do my research.

481
00:38:27,763 --> 00:38:31,809
And if everything looks fine,
I'll sign the agreement.

482
00:38:32,435 --> 00:38:35,271
A woman with a very good head
on her shoulders.

483
00:38:36,439 --> 00:38:37,898
A rare jewel.

484
00:38:39,650 --> 00:38:43,321
Very… very… very rare.

485
00:38:44,572 --> 00:38:49,493
It also helps you're a beautiful woman.

486
00:38:52,496 --> 00:38:54,040
-Thank you, Mr. Congressman.
-[Julio chuckles]

487
00:38:56,375 --> 00:38:59,295
[Julio] Oh. Right on time!

488
00:38:59,378 --> 00:39:02,798
Now that we're done
talking about business…

489
00:39:03,758 --> 00:39:05,509
we can enjoy dinner.

490
00:39:05,593 --> 00:39:07,970
Ivy, do you like steak?

491
00:39:08,679 --> 00:39:11,515
You know, if there's
one thing you should learn about

492
00:39:11,599 --> 00:39:14,435
this whole family, it's that we love meat.

493
00:39:14,518 --> 00:39:15,394
-[Ivy chuckles]
-What about you?

494
00:39:15,478 --> 00:39:16,645
Kinda.

495
00:39:17,480 --> 00:39:20,816
But it has to taste good.

496
00:39:20,900 --> 00:39:22,401
[sensual music playing]

497
00:39:22,485 --> 00:39:24,320
[Julio laughs]

498
00:39:26,155 --> 00:39:27,239
[Julio] Touché.

499
00:39:28,532 --> 00:39:30,117
-Hello.
-Good evening, sir!

500
00:39:31,160 --> 00:39:36,248
[Ivy] You know, Congressman,
I think Mr. Mayor took after you.

501
00:39:36,332 --> 00:39:37,917
A true visionary.

502
00:39:38,000 --> 00:39:42,463
It runs in the blood.
Your grandsons took after you.

503
00:39:43,464 --> 00:39:45,216
[Julio] If you're talking about Arnaldo,

504
00:39:45,299 --> 00:39:47,301
then yes, he took after me.

505
00:39:47,385 --> 00:39:48,594
I'm proud to say.

506
00:39:49,595 --> 00:39:53,224
But didn't you introduce me
to your brother the other day?

507
00:39:53,307 --> 00:39:54,934
-Where is he?
-[Julio] Well…

508
00:39:55,017 --> 00:39:56,310
He's busy, very busy.

509
00:39:56,394 --> 00:40:01,190
He's always busy with whatever he's doing.

510
00:40:01,273 --> 00:40:04,735
Anyway, I don't see any way

511
00:40:04,819 --> 00:40:08,656
how he can improve tonight's company.

512
00:40:09,281 --> 00:40:11,909
Believe me, Ivy.
You're not missing anything.

513
00:40:12,701 --> 00:40:15,454
You see, in every family…

514
00:40:15,538 --> 00:40:17,665
there always has to be someone who's…

515
00:40:18,749 --> 00:40:21,961
Um… How do you put it nicely?

516
00:40:23,129 --> 00:40:24,338
-Weak.
-Dad.

517
00:40:25,339 --> 00:40:29,135
[tense music playing]

518
00:40:33,347 --> 00:40:34,598
[Julio] Uh…

519
00:40:34,682 --> 00:40:36,934
Let's not talk about him.

520
00:40:39,437 --> 00:40:43,274
But then, Arnaldo has more than made up…

521
00:40:44,108 --> 00:40:46,152
for that boy's shortcomings.

522
00:40:47,945 --> 00:40:51,824
And proof of that is you, my dear, Ivy.

523
00:40:52,867 --> 00:40:58,247
You are here with us tonight
because of Arnaldo.

524
00:41:04,753 --> 00:41:06,797
[tense music playing]

525
00:41:09,049 --> 00:41:10,634
[grunts]

526
00:41:11,510 --> 00:41:13,929
[grunting]

527
00:41:14,013 --> 00:41:16,724
[Ivy] <i>Your grandsons took after you.</i>

528
00:41:16,807 --> 00:41:19,852
[Julio] <i>If you're talking</i>
<i>about Arnaldo, then yes.</i>

529
00:41:19,935 --> 00:41:22,021
[Ivy] <i>But didn't you</i>
<i>introduce me to your brother</i>

530
00:41:22,104 --> 00:41:23,189
<i>the other day?</i>

531
00:41:23,272 --> 00:41:24,732
[Julio] <i>He's busy, very busy.</i>

532
00:41:24,815 --> 00:41:31,197
<i>I don't see any way how he can</i>
<i>improve tonight's company.</i>

533
00:41:31,280 --> 00:41:34,283
<i>You see, in every family…</i>

534
00:41:34,366 --> 00:41:36,076
<i>there always has to be someone who's…</i>

535
00:41:36,160 --> 00:41:41,582
-[Diego grunts]
-[Julio] <i>…weak.</i>

536
00:41:41,665 --> 00:41:43,792
[Diego grunting]

537
00:41:51,467 --> 00:41:53,802
I won't allow you to go home by yourself.

538
00:41:53,886 --> 00:41:55,679
I can drive you home.

539
00:41:59,433 --> 00:42:01,060
If you insist, Mr. Mayor.

540
00:42:01,143 --> 00:42:03,354
Okay. Let me get my keys.

541
00:42:03,437 --> 00:42:06,857
Uh, wait. I think I need
to use the restroom.

542
00:42:06,941 --> 00:42:08,984
Sure. This way.

543
00:42:10,069 --> 00:42:11,779
Okay. Excuse me.

544
00:42:34,218 --> 00:42:38,556
["Sa'Yo" instrumental playing]

545
00:43:52,546 --> 00:43:53,881
I'm sorry.

546
00:43:53,964 --> 00:43:58,594
I was looking for the restroom.
I opened the wrong door.

547
00:44:07,019 --> 00:44:07,853
Sorry.

548
00:44:14,902 --> 00:44:18,530
["Sa'Yo" by Silent Sanctuary playing]

549
00:45:09,164 --> 00:45:10,290
Ivy, wait.

550
00:45:13,001 --> 00:45:16,964
I've been thinking about this
since we met at the tournament.

551
00:45:20,717 --> 00:45:21,885
You look familiar.

552
00:45:26,056 --> 00:45:27,683
Have we met before?

553
00:45:28,642 --> 00:45:34,356
["Sa'Yo" by Silent Sanctuary playing]

554
00:45:49,788 --> 00:45:52,541
<i>Hello, friends!</i>

555
00:45:52,624 --> 00:45:56,753
[Loring] <i>I guess Ms. Ivy's one</i>
<i>of the governor's friends now.</i>

556
00:45:56,837 --> 00:45:59,047
<i>I must've had the wrong impression of her.</i>

557
00:45:59,131 --> 00:45:59,965
<i>Babe!</i>

558
00:46:00,048 --> 00:46:02,551
[Carlotta] <i>You're looking</i>
<i>for justice, right?</i>

559
00:46:02,634 --> 00:46:05,304
<i>It'll take you a while</i>
<i>before you find evidence.</i>

560
00:46:05,387 --> 00:46:09,683
<i>But if you're after revenge,</i>
<i>it's as quick as one bullet.</i>

561
00:46:09,766 --> 00:46:12,311
<i>Hello? I have a job for you.</i>

562
00:46:15,272 --> 00:46:18,025
<i>The Ardiente family will be gone.</i>

563
00:46:18,108 --> 00:46:19,443
<i>[man] Emilia Ardiente-Torillo!</i>

564
00:46:19,526 --> 00:46:20,861
<i>Your days are over!</i>

565
00:46:20,944 --> 00:46:23,363
[theme music playing]
